	<section>
		<h2>The one guarantee</h2>
		<p>
			Every statement squill rewrites is re-lexed and compared against its
			input. The output must produce the same tokens — allowing only named,
			verified transforms like keyword case — and must keep every comment. On
			any mismatch squill emits your original bytes untouched.
		</p>
		<p>
			So a statement squill does not fully understand is passed through rather
			than mangled, and output is never less correct than input. Run with{" "}
			<code>--strict</code> to turn those passthroughs into a failure once you
			expect squill to understand everything in your tree.
		</p>
	</section>
